<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2012/Tree-study.jpg" alt="This oil sketch features a solitary tree with fall foliage" width="500" height="482" /></p>
<p>A small painting from the early fall at Ebenezer Church Rd just north of Bloomfield, VA. &nbsp;What drew me to paint the tree were the shadows that the branches were casting on the trunk.</p>
<p>I worked in an impressionistic style to prevent the foliage from looking overworked, although the trunk required a lot of going back and forth with a painting knife to get the right effect. I tried to suppress the greens as much as possible relying instead on yellows and blues in the canopy to convey some sense of optical mixing.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Oil on linen 12"x12"</p>